language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Put a plus or minus sign before each of the 19 integers so that the signed values add up to the total.
given arr : matrix indexed by [int(1..19)] of int(-100000..100000)
given total : int(-100000000..100000000)
find result : matrix indexed by [int(1..19)] of int(-100000..100000)

such that
$ each signed entry is the integer itself or its negation, i.e. the sign of each integer is chosen
forAll i : int(1..19) . (result[i] = arr[i] \/ result[i] = -arr[i]),
$ the signed integers sum to the total
(sum i : int(1..19) . result[i]) = total
